2026-04-08 21:42:46    Methodology
2026-04-08 21:42:46    ───────────
2026-04-08 21:42:46    • Projected latency uses the Roofline Model, not a Mac CPU scaling factor.
2026-04-08 21:42:46      compute_time = MACs×2 / (peak_GFLOPS × η),  memory_time = bytes / (peak_BW × η)
2026-04-08 21:42:46      projected = max(compute_time, memory_time)  → bottleneck: compute-bound
2026-04-08 21:42:46    • Device: Snapdragon 778G / Apple A14 Bionic
2026-04-08 21:42:46      Peak CPU: 6.0 GFLOPS FP32  | BW: 34.1 GB/s  | η=0.4
2026-04-08 21:42:46    • Model MACs: 87.82M  |  Memory footprint: 1.57 MB
2026-04-08 21:42:46    • Real-time threshold: 6000 ms  (window=300 samples @ 50.0 Hz)
2026-04-08 21:42:46    • CoreML on Apple Silicon: benchmark IS the Neural Engine measurement.
2026-04-08 21:42:46    • ONNX INT8: weight bytes halved, INT8 throughput modelled as 2× FP32 SIMD.
2026-04-08 21:42:46    • For Android: export ONNX → ONNX Runtime Mobile or TFLite (onnx-tf).
